Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 01:34:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] 034 B2 (TKOffset): vanishing blends ending on sharp
 edges, rim faces meet removed faces beyond their edges

Class: a connected set of faces whose offset vanishes (smallest principal
offset factor 1 - d*k_i <= 0 over the whole face) bounded not only by
tangent edges but also by SHARP edges whose two face offsets intersect
(a convex edge of an inward offset, a concave edge of an outward one):
a box with only its vertical edges filleted, a fillet on one edge, top
edges filleted over sharp vertical edges, fillets on a non-right prism,
shelled inward with a wall thicker than the fillet radius (the default
PartDesign Thickness direction). Before, such a set was out of scope and
the offset was an error.

- findVanishing034b: a neighbour across a sharp edge without a tube is a
  rim face (the rim lemma holds: the offsets of such an edge's points are
  never on the offset); a tube edge on the boundary of the set or at one
  of its vertices keeps the set out of scope (the tube folds as well).
- BRepOffset_Inter3d::ConnexIntByArc: the sharp edge between a vanishing
  face and a rim face is skipped (the vanishing face has no offset).
- Thick solids: the offset edge of a rim face on the removed face (and the
  offset edges it shared with the vanishing face) end where the set was;
  the rim faces meet the removed face and each other beyond that end, and
  exactly at it when the offset equals the blend radius. These edges are
  no longer used (ToContext, ContextIntByArc incl. its vertex fallback);
  the removed face is intersected with enlarged copies of the rim faces
  next to the set (rim pairs, now only for rim faces next to a set face
  that reaches that removed face). This makes the threshold d = r exact
  for thick solids too.
- A planar removed face replaced by a plane face (planar substitution)
  loses its orientation (the plane face is FORWARD): the removed face's
  copy used for the rim-pair intersection gets the orientation of the
  face it replaced, so the section edges on the rim faces are oriented as
  for an analytic plane (B-spline boxes shelled through a vanishing set
  were an error before).
- The stage A/A2 guards and the positive-volume check are unchanged; the
  Inter3d skips are active only while a vanishing set is being handled
  (the stock flow is unchanged otherwise).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
